 rotect Burlington Beach while learning about the importance of keeping our
  shoreline healthy and litter-free.\n\nJoin us for a morning of environmen
 tal action as we search for and remove microplastics and nurdles—tiny pl
 astic pieces that can harm wildlife and enter our waterways.\n\nHosted by:
  BurlingtonGreen\nWhen: Saturday\, August 15th\, 2026 from 9:30 a.m. – 1
 1:30 a.m.\nWhere: Burlington Beach – meet at BG’s Eco-Hub ( (https://g
 .co/kgs/3ANJBcH) 1094 Lakeshore Road)\n\nNote: Please register in advance\
 , using the form below.\n\nWhether you’re a student\, family\, educator\
 , or community member\, this is a great opportunity to wrap up the summer 
 by giving back to nature\, connecting with others\, and helping create a c
 leaner\, healthier shoreline for everyone.\n\nWhy join?\n\n* Help keep Bur
 lington Beach clean and beautiful\n* Make a positive environmental impact 
 before heading back to school\n* Learn about plastic pollution and shoreli
 ne stewardship\n* Connect with fellow community members who care about the
